+Feature: Order of checks on the contract manager backend
+  CM answers with the first failed check: API key (401) first, then the
+  format of path ids, then media type and JSON syntax, then the record the
+  operation needs (404), then body fields, party and state (D84, PSO run).
+  Only the order the digest fixes is tested: 401 before everything else, and
+  404 before body fields and party.
+
+  Background:
+    Given fresh negotiation ids
+
+  @openapi-only @pso-spec @D84 @D65 @D20 @D11 @rbac
+  Scenario: A create call at the Provider with an empty body and no API key gives 401, not 400
+    When I send "POST" to the provider CM at "/credentials/agreements/${aid}/definitions/${did}/create" without an API key
+    Then the response is a problem with status 401 and type "unauthorized"
+    And the problem body follows the error rules of D11
+
+  @openapi-only @pso-spec @D84 @D65 @D25 @D12 @rbac
+  Scenario: A validate-and-sign call for unknown ids gives 401 without a key and 404 with it
+    When I send "POST" to the provider CM at "/credentials/agreements/${aid}/definitions/${did}/issue" without an API key
+    Then the response is a problem with status 401 and type "unauthorized"
+    When I send "POST" to the provider CM at "/credentials/agreements/${aid}/definitions/${did}/issue" with JSON:
+      """
+      {}
+      """
+    Then the response is a problem with status 404 and type "notFound"
+
+  @openapi-only @pso-spec @D84 @D65 @D19 @D11 @rbac
+  Scenario: An existence check with an empty body gives 401 without a key and 400 with it
+    When I send "POST" to the provider CM at "/agreements/${nid}/search" without an API key
+    Then the response is a problem with status 401 and type "unauthorized"
+    And the problem body follows the error rules of D11
+    When I send "POST" to the provider CM at "/agreements/${nid}/search" with JSON:
+      """
+      {}
+      """
+    Then the response is a problem with status 400 and type "validationFailure"
+    And the provider has no contract for the negotiation
+
+  @openapi-only @pso-spec @D84 @D65 @D16 @rbac
+  Scenario: A path id that is not a UUID gives 401 when the API key is missing
+    When I send "GET" to the provider CM at "/agreements/not-a-uuid" without an API key
+    Then the response is a problem with status 401 and type "unauthorized"
+
+  @openapi-only @pso-spec @D84 @D12 @D32
+  Scenario: A status change with an empty body for an unknown agreement gives 404, not 400
+    When I send "PATCH" to the provider CM at "/agreements/${aid}/definitions/${did}/status" with JSON:
+      """
+      {}
+      """
+    Then the response is a problem with status 404 and type "notFound"
+
+  @openapi-only @pso-spec @D84 @D12 @D31
+  Scenario: A verification with an empty body for an unknown negotiation at the Provider gives 404, not 400
+    When I send "PUT" to the provider CM at "/verifications/${nid}" with JSON:
+      """
+      {}
+      """
+    Then the response is a problem with status 404 and type "notFound"
+
+  @openapi-only @pso-spec @D84 @D12 @D33
+  Scenario: A status update with an empty body for an unknown negotiation at the Provider gives 404, not 400
+    When I send "PUT" to the provider CM at "/contractOffers/${nid}/update" with JSON:
+      """
+      {}
+      """
+    Then the response is a problem with status 404 and type "notFound"
